The regression's cause remains unresolved. Static inspection confirms that the latest measured candidate changed the shared reduceField wrapper despite preserving its standard arithmetic and percentile-sort semantics. Reusing the frozen raw records also shows material variability in unchanged baseline and original controls. See DIAGNOSIS-PLAN.md for the separate facts, hypotheses and prospective controls.

Candidate-wrapper restores the exact production registry, reducer wrapper, standard arithmetic and transport bodies. Only an import and a shared-absent percentile dispatch inside special are added. The finite-selection helper is copied byte-identically from the unaccepted algorithm stage. This reduces the scope of the source-layout hypothesis; it does not establish a performance benefit.

The source-stable correctness run passed all four processes: 2,910,751 reducer comparisons, 14,240 standard helper comparisons and 48,240 cache comparisons; 3,888 held-out selection and 864 direct-registry comparisons; 9,600 standard/coercion comparisons, 1,920 helper comparisons and 24 mutation/alias checks; plus 63 mandatory fixed-fixture packets and eight instrumented dispatch checks. These are finite replay campaigns, not a new exhaustive or universally independent corpus. The raw inherited driver's original generator-independence wording is retained but does not make this regenerated corpus new. Its bounded-case elapsed diagnostic is correctness evidence and is not a new timed comparative study.

Every observed semantic, cache, alias, caller-mutation and dispatch comparison passed. The application baseline remains unchanged. Full-product, full-parity, universal-correctness, performance acceptance, superiority and candidate integration remain false. No timed comparative study, isolated-memory measurement or profiler ran. A future measurement harness is only proposed, and requires root's source review and fresh coordinated authorizations.
